From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deepak1556 <hop2deep@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 01:16:07 +0900
Subject: fix: use embedder perfetto client when available

Node.js v24.19.0 introduces a standalone perfetto SDK tracing agent which
initializes an in-process backend, creates independent tracing sessions,
and writes pftrace files. Electron already owns a process wide perfetto
client through Chromium, so creating Node.js owned clients in browser,
renderer processes duplicates tracing infrastructure and produces recording
state independent of contentTracing.

Keep Node.js standalone SDK capability behind `node_use_perfetto_sdk` for
ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE.

For embedded Electron processes, do not create Node.js tracing Agent.
Instead, register Node.js TrackEvent data source with Chromium
perfetto client. This preserves node.* event emission while
allowing contentTracing to remain the sole owner of category filtering,
recording sessions, output, and lifecycle.

diff --git a/node.gni b/node.gni
index a443ff52ca1dda5cb2cfdfe5241076836a33b8fc..7d764d56c5e6318f8faf085b029c994d29ad37ce 100644
--- a/node.gni
+++ b/node.gni
@@ -57,6 +57,10 @@ declare_args() {
   # Initialize v8 platform during node.js startup.
   node_use_v8_platform = false
 
+  # Include Node's standalone Perfetto client. Electron retains it for
+  # ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE while regular Electron processes use Chromium's client.
+  node_use_perfetto_sdk = true
+
   # Custom build tag.
   node_tag = ""
 
